  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A garden map and a host volunteer can explain shared paths, work areas, and gathering places.\", \"decision\": \"How should new visitors understand the shared spaces?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVisitors use the garden map first and ask the host about any unclear shared spaces. The map supports self-guided orientation with optional help.\nThe host and visitors mark shared spaces on the garden map as they walk together. The written guide develops alongside the introduction.\nThe host gives a short walk through the shared spaces before handing visitors the garden map. The map reinforces places visitors have already seen."
    }
